    {
      "id": "eof-modes-and-pdo-index",
      "severity": "should",
      "path": "methods/eof-modes-and-pdo-index.md",
      "sha256": "3544f2f552ecd0f41c41eb09edf7012f49ac8421900f2b571b8498d37f2726b1",
      "reason": "The question's whole diagnostic — leading EOF of North Pacific SST anomalies, explained variance, amplitude from the regression pattern on the standardised index, and pattern correlation between sources — is exactly what this fragment defines and constrains.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Anomalies: remove each cell's annual cycle and the global-mean SST anomaly, then weight by sqrt(cos(latitude)) before the EOF; fix the EOF sign so that positive index = negative SST anomalies in the central and western North Pacific.",
        "Amplitude = area-weighted RMS of the regression pattern (anomalies regressed on the standardised index, °C per SD), not of the EOF; compare explained variance only between fields on the same grid over the same period. The question's plain spatial Pearson differs from the recommended area-weighted `analyze_correlation(weighting='area')`: the question's version is followed and the difference stated."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices",
      "severity": "must",
      "path": "methods/anomaly-baselines-and-climate-indices.md",
      "sha256": "e0afb5c187aca1e075f9549153b1e896320bb0539544f66d3293fab4b4b77c92",
      "reason": "The PDO is defined here against a 1950-2014 monthly climatology, and the index's persistence, baseline offsets and season handling determine how the anomalies, autocorrelation and phase transitions must be computed and stated.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "Remove each source's own climatology; an observed climatology put on model output carries the mean-state bias into the index. State the climatology and baseline (both recorded in attrs).",
        "Build the index on the baseline of the published `pdo` series (`base_period`), so the comparison does not carry a constant offset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "common-comparison-mask",
